   "source": {
    "label": "theorem::noisy_depth_lower_bounds_det_depth",
    "number": "Theorem (theorem::noisy_depth_lower_bounds_det_depth)",
    "quote": "There exist universal constants $c, \\bar{c} > 0$ such that for every integer $K \\ge 2$ there exists a function class $\\F \\subseteq [0,1]^{\\A}$ with action space $|\\A | = K+1$ such that for every $\\epsilon \\in [0,1/2)$ it holds that $\\gamma_{\\F, \\epsilon} = 1/K$ and if $\\sigma^2 \\geq \\frac{1}{\\bar{c}K^{2/3}}$ then $\\bar{c} K^{2/3} \\sigma^2 \\leq \\depth_{\\epsilon, 1/4}^\\sigma(\\F) \\leq c \\log^{2/3}(K) K^{2/3}\\sigma^2.$"
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Theorem also states c_bar log(1/gamma) sigma^2 <= QC. K here: number of non-informative arms (|A|=K+1)."
